{
  "selected_candidate_id": "plan_1",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "candidate_id": "plan_1",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "Google offered the attached Magnifica Start at $579.99, Chefman at $329.99, and Philips 3300 at $729.95. Its accompanying message reports a grinder and manual frother for the Start; a grinder, steam wand, tamper and milk pitcher for Chefman; and LatteGo for Philips. These are reported page claims, not independent verification. Please explain whether your $599.99 Ninja meaningfully improves my two-drink morning routine and expected ownership experience over these alternatives, and whether your cheaper options offer comparable satisfaction. Use your existing facts to clarify the Ninja's milk operation, necessary inclusions and seller identity where possible. I accept manual steaming and do not value unrelated coffee modes for this purchase. You said your catalog has no standalone grinders or accessories, so focus on useful integrated alternatives. Return any additional catalog offers that improve this comparison. My $800 complete-equipment ceiling remains unchanged; savings matter when likely satisfaction is similar.",
        "google": "Bing offered the attached Ninja at $599.99, Breville Impress at $649.99, and VEVOR automatic at $349.99. Its message reports an integrated scale, 25-setting grinder and hands-free frothing for Ninja, but also conflicting manual-frothing copy; it reports automatic milk frothing and a removable milk reservoir for VEVOR. These are reported page claims, not independent verification. Please compare your Magnifica Start and Chefman against Ninja for enjoyable milk drinks, two consecutive morning drinks, cleaning and ownership confidence. Explain when the Impress or Philips premium would materially improve my experience; automatic milk is welcome but not required. Use existing facts to clarify seller attribution, milk-system variant and necessary inclusions where possible. If your catalog contains an espresso-capable standalone grinder, return it so the $299.95 Bambino can become a complete alternative within $800, including necessary accessories. Otherwise prioritize complete integrated options. Return useful additional offers, with frozen prices unchanged."
      },
      "preference_rank": 1,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Shares selected competing offers and accurately attributed public claims. Reiterates the true budget and relevant preferences without promising a purchase or imposing a lower ceiling. Does not forward redundant listings or the entire rival reply.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Bing has an incentive to defend Ninja against Google's cheaper automatic and budget choices. Google has an incentive to explain its alternatives or expose a useful grinder to win a complete or partial purchase. Both may emphasize favorable differences while leaving uncertainties unresolved.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Balances discovery with focused comparison of plausible finalists across prices. It tests whether convenience and confidence justify premiums while preserving cheaper offers and a possible separate setup.",
      "shared_record_ids": {
        "bing": [
          "google-3210de58f63aae1163cd",
          "google-73d649a23e17eb409d3e",
          "google-0572500f0732845cad88"
        ],
        "google": [
          "bing-43de8e4359ad1784cba0",
          "bing-d2b74b50a379b8bf71a0",
          "bing-78a4158303ba5999efdb"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "candidate_id": "plan_2",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "Google's attached Chefman costs $329.99; its message reports an espresso grinder, steam wand, 120V operation, tamper and milk pitcher. Its card advertises 90-day returns, though seller attribution and applicability remain uncertain. Please compare your $189.99 CUSIMAX and $349.99 VEVOR with that complete-setup prospect. Identify supported reasons to expect acceptable drink consistency, manageable cleaning and seller recourse, distinguishing unknowns from defects. Return any other credible lower-cost complete options in your catalog. I can still spend up to $800 total when the improvement justifies it; this is a value comparison, not a new spending cap. Explain the strongest reason to retain Ninja or Impress instead.",
        "google": "Bing's attached CUSIMAX costs $189.99 and VEVOR costs $349.99. Its message reports a conical grinder and steam wand for CUSIMAX and automatic grinding and milk preparation for VEVOR, while noting uncertainty about durability and recourse. Please explain whether your $329.99 Chefman offers a worthwhile improvement in expected satisfaction or confidence over these offers. Use existing facts about the actual seller, necessary inclusions and advertised returns without treating aggregate merchant labels as seller confirmation. Return other credible lower-cost complete alternatives if available, and explain the strongest practical reason to pay more for your Start or Impress. My true ceiling remains $800 total; I have not decided to buy the cheapest qualifying setup."
      },
      "preference_rank": 2,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Makes savings salient without inventing a hard budget or claiming low-cost offers are equivalent. Shares only budget competitors and keeps higher-priced first-round offers available.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Providers may offer cheaper substitutes to avoid losing the purchase, but their revenue incentive also encourages defending higher-priced machines through claimed quality or convenience.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Could uncover strong inexpensive options and sharpen the premium justification. It gives less attention to workflow differences among the more established midrange candidates.",
      "shared_record_ids": {
        "bing": [
          "google-73d649a23e17eb409d3e"
        ],
        "google": [
          "bing-b79dd022ff37659d63c9",
          "bing-78a4158303ba5999efdb"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "candidate_id": "plan_3",
      "messages": {
        "bing": "Google returned the attached $649.95 Impress and $579.99 Magnifica Start. Please focus on your Ninja and Impress: explain the likely practical differences in shot preparation, milk preparation, cleanup and learning for two consecutive morning drinks. Use your available facts to resolve material model, seller or inclusion ambiguity where possible, especially Ninja's mixed frothing descriptions. Google's Impress card advertises 30-day returns but has an aggregate merchant label; its four-cent price advantage alone will not determine my choice. Return any catalog alternative that offers a better balance of workflow and ownership confidence. The ceiling remains $800 for the complete setup, and manual steaming is acceptable.",
        "google": "Bing returned the attached $599.99 Ninja and $649.99 Impress. Please compare these with your Start, Impress and Philips for my two consecutive milk drinks, including daily preparation, milk-system cleaning and learning effort. Bing reports conflicting manual and hands-free frothing descriptions for Ninja, so treat its exact operation as unresolved. Explain what the Philips premium buys and whether it is likely worthwhile when I am happy to steam manually. Use existing facts to clarify your exact Philips variant, actual sellers, advertised recourse and required accessory inclusions. Return useful alternatives if available. My $800 total ceiling is unchanged; higher spending needs a practical benefit."
      },
      "preference_rank": 3,
      "disclosure_and_withholding": "Shares midrange competitors and emphasizes existing workflow and seller-confidence preferences. Does not claim a preference for premium equipment or discard budget offers.",
      "anticipated_recommender_behavior": "Both providers are likely to defend their higher-value purchases with convenience and reputation arguments. The nearly identical Impress prices may shift discussion toward seller attribution, although available facts may not resolve it.",
      "expected_user_value_tradeoff": "Provides a focused comparison of likely convenient options, but risks encouraging premium recommendations and missing a satisfying cheaper or separate setup.",
      "shared_record_ids": {
        "bing": [
          "google-ae16f17e37b151e3a9fd",
          "google-3210de58f63aae1163cd"
        ],
